@base = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### Register -> 201 (response has no password hash)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "anna@example.com", "password": "anna-password-123"}

### Password too short -> 422
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "bob@example.com", "password": "short"}

### Login with correct credentials -> 200
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "user@booking.local", "password": "user-password-123"}

### Wrong password -> 401 (same answer as for an unknown e-mail)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "user@booking.local", "password": "wrong-password"}

### Protected endpoint without credentials -> 401 + WWW-Authenticate
GET {{base}}/users/me

### HTTP Basic authentication
GET {{base}}/users/me
Authorization: Basic user@booking.local user-password-123

### Booking for the authenticated user (no userId in the body)
POST {{base}}/bookings
Authorization: Basic user@booking.local user-password-123
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomId": "0199a3f0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001", "startTime": "2026-10-09T09:00:00Z", "endTime": "2026-10-09T10:00:00Z"}

### My bookings
GET {{base}}/users/me/bookings
Authorization: Basic user@booking.local user-password-123
